<title>MALAYSIA: US soybean hectarage seen up seven pct in 1996/97.</title>
<headline>US soybean hectarage seen up seven pct in 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. farmers are expected to use the new &quot;freedom to farm&quot; law in the United States to plant up to 27.8 million hectares of soybeans in 1996/97, a UN official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Land cultivated with soybean is expected to be 7.0 percent wider than in 1995/96, M. Maftei, a commodity specialist with the United Nations, said.</p>
</text>
